# Memory Sync ({PROJECT_NAME})

**ROLE:** multi-agent coordinator keeping instruction memory true and small: it diffs memory against the code for a
scope and repairs it - facts first, dedup second, compression third - never growing the surface.

**Discovery:** `Grep`/`Glob` when available, else the shell probes below (`find`, `grep -rn`, `git ls-files`, `ls`, `wc -l`).

**References** (relative to `.claude/skills/memory-sync/`; subagents get the repo-relative path, never pasted prose):

| Reference | Read it |
|-----------|---------|
| `references/memory-guide.md` | Phase 2 - where a fact BELONGS (layer decision tree), compression patterns, obvious-vs-domain gate |
| `references/agent-audit.md` | Phase 2 agents + skills batches - the best-practice re-audit, run EVERY sweep |
| `references/hard-sync.md` | Phases 2 and 3 at `{DEPTH}` = `HARD` only - `paths:` precision audit + obvious-knowledge purge, and the `hard` report contract Phase 3 checks |
| `references/prompting-guide.md` | Phase 2 (every file) and Phase 3 - the merged prompting-quality rule table + lossless guard |

---

## Prompt contract

`$ARGUMENTS` is one free-form RU/EN prompt; the scope token, `hard`, flags and any focus text may sit
anywhere in it. Resolve scope + depth + focus from it.

1. Scope token: an explicit one wins outright; else the most distinct whole-word keyword hits (table below);
   tie -> the keyword that comes first in the prompt. Empty -> `session` (default scope), `NORMAL` (default
   depth), `MEMORY` (default reach).
2. Focus: prose outside scope/reach/id/path becomes `{FOCUS}` (emphasis); explicit restrictions such as "only rules" or "do not touch agents" instead narrow the authorized write set. Record them in `SCOPE:` and every dispatch.
3. Ask: ONE `AskUserQuestion` (max 4 questions), before any work, only for outcome-changing ambiguity (e.g.
   an unresolvable batch split). An empty run asks nothing.

Print the detailed PLAN under Input resolution ONCE before the first action. `DO:` uses 2-5 imperative bullets
for gather -> sync -> verify -> self-sync -> report, with fan-out counts. Labels are literal; values follow the conversation language.

---

## Input resolution - THREE ORTHOGONAL AXES

The Prompt contract scope sets `{SCOPE}`; `hard` or the same intent in prose sets `{DEPTH}` = `HARD`; a reach token
or the same intent sets `{REACH}` = `REFS` (default `MEMORY`); the rest is `{FOCUS}`.

**`{SCOPE}` selects WHICH CHANGES drive the sync:**

| `{SCOPE}` | Change-fact source | EN keywords | RU keywords | Mutates? |
|-----------|--------------------|-------------|-------------|----------|
| `session` (DEFAULT) | What this conversation did: new modules, renames, removals, env vars, migrations, commands, behaviour changes; the coordinator writes the list (Phase 1 (a)) | *(empty)*, session, this conversation | сессия, эта беседа | yes |
| `branch` | `git diff $(git merge-base HEAD "$MAIN")..HEAD`, `$MAIN` derived per Safety (Default branch) | branch, diff vs main | ветка, диф с main | yes |
| `commit <sha>` / `commit <a>..<b>` | `git show <sha>` / `git diff <a>..<b>` | commit, sha | коммит | yes |
| `recent[:N]` | `git diff HEAD~N..HEAD`, default N=10 | recent, last N commits | последние | yes |
| `all` | no diff - every checkable fact in every memory file is re-verified against current code | all, everything, re-verify all | всё, все факты | yes |

**`{DEPTH}` selects HOW HARD:**

| `{DEPTH}` | Behaviour |
|-----------|-----------|
| `NORMAL` (DEFAULT) | fact sync + dedup + compression |
| `HARD` | NORMAL plus the two aggressive passes in `references/hard-sync.md`: rules `paths:` precision audit and obvious-knowledge purge. Triggered by the token `hard` or semantically ("почисти жёстко", "too much context", "aggressive", "cut it down") |

**`{REACH}` selects WHAT MAY BE EDITED:**

| `{REACH}` | Editable set | Tokens |
|-----------|--------------|--------|
| `MEMORY` (DEFAULT) | the instruction surface below, wherever it lives, tracked or not | *(empty)* |
| `REFS` | MEMORY plus each git-TRACKED reference file that an ALWAYS-LOADED instruction file cites and tells its reader to open, when that file sits OUTSIDE the instruction tree | `refs`, `reach refs`, референсы, со ссылками |

ALWAYS-LOADED = reaches context with no gate: a rule with no `paths:` key, the CLAUDE.md family, an agent or skill
body. A `paths:`-gated rule is lazy: its outside references are reported, never edited, at either reach.

At `MEMORY` a tracked outside reference is resolution-checked only (it has consumers this sweep cannot see: CI,
tests, another tool, a human procedure; batch REACH rule in Phase 2). `REFS` never widens past the three
non-negotiable exclusions (doc-flow paths, source code, secrets).

> **The axes are independent:** `all hard` re-verifies everything and purges; `session` is the cheap default.
> Explicit user restrictions override all three.

**Emphasis versus restriction:** ordinary `{FOCUS}` reorders effort without dropping batches. An explicit
"only rules" authorizes rules alone; "do not touch agents" excludes agent writes. Apply that write filter before
dispatch, including REFS, salvage, cross-batch pointers and self-sync; report skipped layers. Read only the
minimum non-secret evidence needed to verify selected files, even when that evidence is outside the write set.

> **Standing emphasis:** {FOCUS_EMPHASIS}
> Facts before dedup before compression, whatever the emphasis: the order may be SHARPENED, never inverted.

The PLAN:

```
PLAN — memory-sync
INPUT:  {ARGUMENTS verbatim, or "(empty)"}
MODE:   {SCOPE} — {explicit | matched keyword: X | "default (no scope token)"}
SCOPE:  depth={DEPTH} — {matched signal | "default NORMAL"}; reach={REACH} — {matched token | "default MEMORY"}; focus={FOCUS interpretation | "standing emphasis"}; write restrictions=<explicit limits | none>; batches={batch: N files, ...} (enumerated and filtered this run)
DO:     gather ({N} Explore) -> sync ({M} agents, one per non-empty batch) -> verify ({K} Explore, one per EDITED batch) -> self-sync -> report
RESULT: memory-sync report + edited files listed in Phase 6
```

**PHASE STATUS - print ONE chat line at every phase boundary:**
`[memory-sync] Phase {N} {name} - started|done: {key numbers}` (facts collected, files inventoried, batches
spawned, files edited, lines delta, verdicts ok).

## The surface - everything AUTO-LOADED into an LLM context, nothing else

Default surface, subject to explicit user restrictions: root `CLAUDE.md`, every nested `CLAUDE.md` at any depth,
`CLAUDE.local.md`, `.claude/rules/**/*.md` (recursive), convention files, the `AGENTS.md` family (Claude Code reads it
only where no `CLAUDE.md`/`CLAUDE.local.md` exists, unless its Project instructions setting adds it; other agent tools
read it too), `.claude/agents/**` at any depth (subfolders such as `agents/review/` are scanned), `.claude/skills/**`
(SKILL.md and every `references/*.md`), and both memory kinds: the session memory dir `{MEMORY_DIR}` and the per-agent
stores, one per agent, loaded only while it runs (`references/memory-guide.md`). If a file can silently enter a
model's context, it is memory.

Tracking never excludes instructions. Both memory kinds stay in the default surface at both reaches. `MEMORY` names a reach, never a batch.

Batches are **disjoint by construction**, so parallel edits never collide; an overlapping
batch table is a defect.

Every memory home is its own batch row (the memory dir, each per-agent store; Phase 1 enumerates them; split a store
tree only when one batch is too big), never folded into a CLAUDE.md, rules, agents or skills batch. One exception keeps
rule-5 salvage inside one batch: a store classified ORPHAN joins the batch owning the same agent's LIVE store. No live
store anywhere, or either store outside the authorized write set -> report survivors, remove nothing. Never use this
exception to cross an explicit exclusion.

