## NON-GROWTH - the prime directive

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Budget | Each file <= baseline and TOTAL delta <= 0, except HARD PASS A `paths:` repair on a MISSING/TOO_NARROW verdict and verified rule-5 salvage into the SAME agent's authorized live store in the SAME owned batch. Salvage recipient growth <= removed-store lines; TOTAL delta still <= 0. A positive delta is stated first (Phase 6) |
| Order | **DELETE** (duplicate / obvious / stale / dead) -> **COMPRESS** -> **MOVE** to the right layer -> **ADD** last. Never add before cutting |
| Longest first | Rank the surface by `wc -l` and compress the top files hardest. Report the top-5 before/after. A long rules file is a bug, not thoroughness |
| Add gate | A new fact enters only if all hold: non-obvious for a competent model, domain-specific to {PROJECT_NAME}, verified against a real source, and its absence costs a real failure. It must earn its line by displacing another |
| Traceable | Every surviving claim maps to a file, command output or commit. Verify uncertain claims; still uncertain -> leave and report. Delete only proven stale or disallowed claims |
| Authority | On conflict: rules + CLAUDE.md beat memory; a nested CLAUDE.md beats the root one for its own subtree |
| Edit only | Targeted `Edit` diffs, bottom-up by line number. Never `Write` a whole memory file |

Never add the obvious ("write good code", "follow SOLID", "add tests", "handle errors", "do not hardcode secrets",
restated tool or framework docs); add domain facts, environment quirks, mistakes actually hit and their cause.
Decision tree: `references/memory-guide.md`.

