## Phase 4 - SELF-SYNC (the skill syncs itself)

After Phase 3, self-sync only files allowed by the user's write restrictions; otherwise report it skipped. Spawn
one independent read-only checker over the self-synced files (this SKILL.md and the authorized references),
reported as its own row in the Phase-6 delta table:

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| Re-enumerate | Re-run the Phase 1 enumeration and compare with the batch table and surface counts, after subtracting this skill's own files (`.claude/skills/memory-sync/**`): the snapshot predates this skill, so counting them reports a phantom `+N` drift every run |
| Refresh | Update the batch rows, the counts, every fact-catalogue command that no longer matches reality, and the runtime-seat roster's call-site lines (they rot fastest) |
| Grow a batch | The project gained a memory layer this skill does not cover (a new nested `CLAUDE.md` tree, a new convention dir, a new skills tree) -> add the batch or the section, report it |
| Drop a batch | A batch whose files are all gone -> remove the row and say so in the report |
| Sibling refs | Authorized members of the four references (`memory-guide.md`, `agent-audit.md`, `hard-sync.md`, `prompting-guide.md`) follow the same self-sync; their rosters, patterns and checks also drift |

> **CARVE-OUT:** batch agents correct facts but never change scope decisions (surface, EXCLUDED table, docs exclusion,
> non-growth directive) without explicit user instruction. The coordinator may add/drop Phase-4 batches within
> authorized scope and reports them; those lines are total-delta-exempt.

